.TH MU2E 4 "2026-10-06" "mu2e-pcie-utils 9.01.00" "Mu2e DAQ Manual"
.SH NAME
mu2e \- Mu2e DTC/CFO PCIe card driver and its /dev/mu2eN device nodes
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include \(dqmu2e_driver/mu2e_mmap_ioctl.h\(dq
.PP
.BI /dev/mu2e N
.RI ( N " = 0 .. 3)"
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B mu2e
kernel module
.RI ( mu2e.ko ,
built from
.IR mu2e_driver/ )
binds Xilinx PCI devices 10ee:7042 and 10ee:7043 (DTC and CFO firmware).
It allocates a character-device region named
.B mu2e_drv
with
.B MU2E_MAX_NUM_DTCS
= 4 minors, a device class
.BR mu2e_dev ,
and one node
.BI mu2e N
per probed card.
The minor number is the card index used everywhere else
.RB ( \-d ,
.BR DTCLIB_DTC ,
.BR \-\-dtc ).
.PP
The file operations are
.BR open ,
.BR release ,
.B unlocked_ioctl
and
.BR mmap .
There is no
.BR read (2),
.BR write (2)
or
.BR poll (2),
and no
.B compat_ioctl
(32-bit userspace on a 64-bit kernel is not supported).
.PP
At probe time the driver allocates the DMA rings and writes two registers:
0x9030 (scratch) receives
.BR mu2e_host_hash() ,
the 16-bit TRACE name hash of the host name in bits 31:16 and the card index in
bits 15:0;
0x9188 receives the load time in Unix seconds.
.SS Open and ownership
The first
.BR open (2)
by a process without
.B CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE
records that process's UID as owner and sets the inode owner to it.
While the open count is non-zero, an open by a different UID
(real and effective) fails with
.BR EBUSY .
The last close returns the inode to root.
Processes with
.B CAP_DAC_OVERRIDE
bypass the check and are not counted.
.PP
The driver does not look at the open mode: a descriptor opened
.B O_RDONLY
can write registers through
.BR M_IOC_REG_ACCESS .
Access control therefore rests entirely on the node's mode;
.B setup_dkms.sh
installs the udev rule
.B KERNEL==\(dqmu2e*\(dq, MODE=\(dq0666\(dq
(see
.BR setup_dkms.sh (1)).
.SS Register access
.EX
typedef uint16_t dtc_address_t;
typedef uint32_t dtc_data_t;
typedef struct {
    dtc_address_t reg_offset;   /* byte offset from BAR0          */
    int           access_type;  /* 0 read, 1 write, 2 write+read  */
    dtc_data_t    val;
} m_ioc_reg_access_t;           /* 12 bytes; offsets 0, 4, 8      */
.EE
.PP
Type 0 reads
.IR val ;
type 1 writes and returns without copying back;
type 2 writes then reads back under a single global mutex.
The 16-bit offset limits the reachable space to the first 64 KiB of BAR0, which
holds the NWL DMA engine registers (0x0000\-0x40FF) and the DTC/CFO register map
(0x9000\-0xA454).
The driver checks neither the offset against the BAR length nor its alignment.
.SS ioctl requests
Magic
.BR \(aqC\(aq .
Command values are for Linux x86_64.
.EX
Request              nr dir  argument (size)           cmd value
M_IOC_GET_TST_STATE   1 RW   m_ioc_cmd_t (16)          0xC0104301
M_IOC_TEST_START      2 W    m_ioc_cmd_t (16)          0x40104302
M_IOC_TEST_STOP       3 W    m_ioc_cmd_t (16)          0x40104303
M_IOC_GET_PCI_STATE   4 R    m_ioc_pcistate_t (60)     0x803C4304
M_IOC_GET_ENG_STATE   5 RW   m_ioc_engstate_t (36)     0xC0244305
M_IOC_GET_DMA_STATS   6 RW   m_ioc_engstats_t (16)     0xC0104306
M_IOC_GET_TRN_STATS   7 RW   TRNStatsArray (16)        0xC0104307
M_IOC_REG_ACCESS      9 RW   m_ioc_reg_access_t (12)   0xC00C4309
M_IOC_GET_INFO       12 RW   m_ioc_get_info_t (28)     0xC01C430C
M_IOC_BUF_GIVE       13 none integer                   0x0000430D
M_IOC_DUMP           14 none \-                         0x0000430E
M_IOC_BUF_XMIT       16 none integer                   0x00004310
M_IOC_DCS_LOCK       17 none \-                         0x00004311
M_IOC_DCS_RELEASE    18 none \-                         0x00004312
M_IOC_GET_VERSION    19 R    mu2e_string_t (100)       0x80644313
.EE
.PP
.B M_IOC_GET_DMA_STATS
and
.B M_IOC_GET_TRN_STATS
carry a user pointer, so their size and command value differ on ILP32.
Unknown commands return
.B ENOSYS
(not
.BR ENOTTY );
a wrong magic returns
.BR ENOTTY .
.TP
.B M_IOC_GET_INFO
In:
.IR chn ,
.IR dir ,
.IR tmo_ms .
Out:
.IR buff_size ,
.IR num_buffs ,
.I hwIdx
(hardware ring index) and
.I swIdx
(software index).
The number of filled receive buffers is
.BR mu2e_chn_info_delta_() .
.TP
.B M_IOC_BUF_GIVE
Argument
.BR "(chn << 24) | (dir << 16) | num" :
return
.I num
received buffers to the hardware.
.TP
.B M_IOC_BUF_XMIT
Argument
.BR "(chn << 24) | (bytes & 0xFFFFFF)" :
transmit the S2C buffer at the current software index.
.TP
.BR M_IOC_DCS_LOCK ", " M_IOC_DCS_RELEASE
A per-card test-and-set flag.
.B LOCK
returns
.B EAGAIN
if the flag is set; it never blocks.
.B RELEASE
clears the flag unconditionally; it has no owner and is not cleared when the
holder closes the device or exits.
.TP
.B M_IOC_GET_VERSION
Copies the 100-byte
.B DRIVER_VERSION_STRING
(\(dqv3_00_00\(dq in the source;
.B setup_dkms.sh
replaces it with
.B git describe \-\-tags
of the DKMS source tree).
.TP
.BR M_IOC_DUMP
Writes the ring state to the kernel TRACE buffer or printk.
.SS DMA buffers and mmap
Each card has two DMA channels, 0 = DAQ and 1 = DCS
.RB ( DTC_DMA_Engine ),
each with two directions, C2S = 0 (card to system, receive) and
S2C = 1 (system to card, send).
A receive ring has
.B MU2E_NUM_RECV_BUFFS
= 100 buffers, a send ring
.B MU2E_NUM_SEND_BUFFS
= 60; every buffer is a 64 KiB
.B mu2e_databuff_t
allocated with
.BR dma_alloc_coherent() .
The header also defines
.B SET_DTC_MAX_DMA_SIZE
0xFFF8, which no driver source uses.
Hardware descriptors are the 32-byte packed NWL formats
.B mu2e_buffdesc_C2S_t
and
.B mu2e_buffdesc_S2C_t
.RI ( xdma_hw.h );
they are not mapped to userspace.
.PP
The
.BR mmap (2)
offset selects one region: page index
.IR pg " = " chn "\(mu4 + " dir "\(mu2 + " map ,
computed by
.BR chnDirMap2offset() .
.I map
0
.RB ( MU2E_MAP_BUFF )
is the data-buffer array
.RI ( num_buffs " \(mu " buff_size );
.I map
1
.RB ( MU2E_MAP_META )
is
.I num_buffs
.BR int s
of per-buffer metadata.
.B libDTCInterface
maps buffers with
.B PROT_WRITE
and metadata with
.BR PROT_READ .
.SH FILES
.TP
.BI /dev/mu2e N
Card nodes.
.TP
.I /etc/udev/rules.d/98\-mu2e.rules
Node mode, written by
.BR setup_dkms.sh .
.TP
.I /etc/modules\-load.d/mu2e.conf
Loads the module at boot, written by
.BR setup_dkms.sh .
.TP
.I /lib/modules/*/extra/mu2e.ko
DKMS-installed module (with
.I TRACE.ko
and
.IR pci_devel_main.ko ).
.SH NOTES
The companion module
.B pci_devel_main
.RI ( mcs/basic_driver )
creates
.BI /dev/pcidev N
with magic
.B \(aqD\(aq
(hello, ioremap/iounmap, 32-bit register access, and
.B IOC_IOOP
read/write); it is used only by
.BR mcs (1)
and
.BR devl (1)
to reprogram the configuration PROM.
.SH EXAMPLES
Find the cards and the driver version:
.PP
.EX
ls \-l /dev/mu2e*
DTCRegDump \-d 0 | grep \(aq^Driver Version\(aq
dkms status mu2e_pcie_utils
.EE
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR my_cntl (1),
.BR DTCRegDump (1),
.BR setup_dkms.sh (1),
.BR libDTCInterface (3),
.BR ioctl (2),
.BR mmap (2)
